      "lw $t1,-100($t2)",
      "Load word : Reads the 32-bit (4-byte) value at memory address ($t2 + offset) and places it in $t1. The address must be word-aligned (divisible by 4). Example: 'lw $t0,0($sp)' loads the value at the top of the stack.",
